  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: MCQ_002
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MCQQuestionData
  questionText: What is the correct ratio of aluminium, potassium and sulphate ions
    in a formula unit of potash alum?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: The chemical formula of potash alum is K<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>.Al<sub>2</sub>(SO<sub>4</sub>)<sub>3</sub>.24H<sub>2</sub>O
    or KAl(SO<sub>4</sub>)<sub>2</sub>.12H<sub>2</sub>O. Hence, the ratio of aluminium,
    potassium and sulphate ions in a formula unit of potash alum is 1:1:2.
  options:
  - 1:2:1
  - 2:1:1
  - 2:1:2
  - 1:1:2
  correctOptionIndex: 3
